  "body": "The maintainer asked for this on 2026-11-14: \"Triage all the testings that is done in a release gatea.. It seems excessivly ineffecient with large tests that takes forever that could be broken down into smaller pieces and executed in parallell\".\n\nThe triage is in a comment on issue 1714. A few long tests hold the release gate. Each is one `#[test]` that does several independent pieces of work in sequence.\n\nSplit these tests. Keep every assert.\n\n- `the_sample_as_imported_still_generates_the_3d_finish` in `crates/app/tests/shared_face_bodies.rs` (about 28 min in release). Split it by level band, or give it a lighter fixture band.\n- `every_rotary_kind_reads_the_radial_law_and_its_cost_is_measured` in `rotary_field_parity` (768 s in release). Make one test for each rotary kind and each measure (6 tests).\n- `step_files_agree_or_refuse_by_name` in `crates/kernel/tests/step_agreement.rs` (90 s). Make one test for each STEP file.\n- `whole_model_pocket`, `keep_law`, `level_links` and `lathe_field_sim` (74 s to 125 s each in debug). Split each binary along its test groups.\n\nAlso add the time of each test to the gate summary. The logs show the time of a binary only, so a slow test in a binary is not visible.\n\nRules:\n- The split tests must be able to run in parallel. They must not share mutable state.\n- The asserts and the golden values do not change.\n- Record the `#[test]` count before and after for each file in the PR.\n\nDone means: no single test in the release tier runs longer than 5 minutes on the maintainer's machine, the gate summary lists the 10 slowest tests, and the assert count for each split file is the same or higher.\n\nPart of the gate work in issues 1702, 1703 and 1714.\n",
